          <p>
            Two label quirks are worth knowing. Body Fortress's tub front advertises 60 g of protein because it quotes a two-scoop serving of 90 g; the one-scoop figure of 30 g is the fair comparison. Premier's 30 g needs about two scoops, so one scoop alone gives roughly 15 g. Read the serving line on each tub before you compare.
          </p>

          <p>
            Our database also flags small inconsistencies on the Premier side. Target's panel shows 3 g of carbohydrate, while some grocery listings show 4 g, which may mean a label revision, and Target's description says 160 calories while the panel says 150. We use the panel. Body Fortress adds vitamin C, vitamin D3 and zinc, per its ingredient list; Premier's powder has no vitamin premix.
