          </p>

          <p>
            The weak points show up in our scoring. At 67% protein by weight, with maltodextrin third on the label, it is one of the less dense mainstream blends, and 180 calories per 30 g is the highest of the pair. It contains soy, buyers often find it thick, and its online prices swing wildly, up to about $1.95 per 25 g at Vitacost. That adds up to a Label Score of 51 out of 100.
